ἀργύριον, -ου, τό
(ἄργυρος), [in LXX for כֶּסֶף (Gen.13.2, al.), exc. Lam.4.1 (כֶּתֶם) ;] 
prop., a piece of silver (Lft., Notes, 191); in NT, 
__(a) silver: Act.3.6; 7.16; 19.19; 20.33, 1Co.3.12, 1Pe.1.18; 
__(b) money: Mat.25.18, 27, Mrk.14.11, Luk.9.3; 19.15, 23; 22.5, Act.8.20; 
__(with) a silver coin: p1., Mat.26.15; 27.3-6, 9; 28.12, 15, where the value is that of a shekel or tetradrachm; ἀργυρίου μυριάδες…
